AccessMapView.description:
The effective `role → capabilities` policy (Settings › Access; ADR-009 §1/§5).
`is_default` is true when no admin override is stored (the built-in policy);
`version` is the map version (`0` for the default) that drives session re-auth.

ConnectionView.description:
One environment → `kneo_client` profile mapping (Settings › Connections;
ADR-009 §2). `profile` is `None` when the env uses the client's default resolution.
`version` drives optimistic-concurrency edits.

put.description:
Set the role → allowed-environments grants. Requires `SETTINGS_WRITE` (admin in the built-in default map). Unknown roles are `400`;
a stale `version` (or create-over-existing) is `409`; attempts a best-effort audit append
(persistence not guaranteed). (Admin always retains access to every env, so this can't lock admins out.)
